    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d798">

                <pb facs="1267" n="1253" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1253"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War/10–644</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé to the Czechoslovak Government in Exile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-06">October 6,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received October 14.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of my telegram No. 17 and
                    despatch No. 189 of October 2, 1944<anchor n="39" xml:id="d798-f1"/> reporting
                    the willingness of the Czechoslovak Government to associate itself with a
                    possible declaration by the United Nations warning Germany against a reported
                    plan to exterminate the inmates of certain prison camps, I have the honor to
                    transmit a copy of a note of October 4, 1944<anchor n="40" xml:id="d798-f2"/>
                    from Mr. Jan Masaryk, Czechoslovak Minister of Foreign Affairs, in which he
                    quotes a telegram which he has received on this subject from the World Jewish
                    Congress in New York. On behalf of his Government, Mr. Masaryk also asks the
                    United States Government to consider whether there is any possibility of
                    assisting the internees whose lives are evidently in extreme danger, and adds
                    that he is also approaching the Governments of Great Britain and the Soviet
                    Union on this subject.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rudolf</hi> E. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
